From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nikolajs Agafonovs <nikolajs.agafonovs@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 20 Nov 2026 15:50:40 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] talloc: use va_copy when <stdarg.h> defines it

talloc.c assumed va_copy only for __GNUC__ > 2 and otherwise defined it as
a plain assignment, which does not compile where va_list is an array type
(x86_64).  Compilers that define __GNUC__ as 2 or not at all but have a
C99 <stdarg.h> (tcc) failed with "lvalue expected".  va_copy is a macro
in every C99 <stdarg.h>, so test for it as well.
---
 netsurf/utils/talloc.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/netsurf/utils/talloc.c b/netsurf/utils/talloc.c
index 408e94b..2d79d24 100644
--- a/netsurf/utils/talloc.c
+++ b/netsurf/utils/talloc.c
@@ -55,7 +55,7 @@
 #include "replace.h"
 #else
 #include <stdarg.h>
-#if !defined(__BEOS__) && __GNUC__ > 2
+#if !defined(__BEOS__) && (__GNUC__ > 2 || defined(va_copy))
 /* Assume we've got va_copy */
 #define HAVE_VA_COPY
 #include <string.h>
